---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const papers = [
  { name: 'MapReduce', what: 'Batch processing as map and reduce functions, with the framework handling distribution and failures.' },
  { name: 'HDFS', what: 'A distributed file system built for large files, streaming reads, and commodity hardware.' },
  { name: 'Bigtable', what: 'A sparse, sorted, distributed map: the design behind many wide-column stores.' },
  { name: 'ZooKeeper', what: 'A coordination service for configuration, leader election, and locks in distributed systems.' },
  { name: 'Kafka', what: 'A distributed log for high-throughput messaging and stream processing.' },
  { name: 'Spark', what: 'Resilient distributed datasets: in-memory cluster computing with lineage-based fault tolerance.' },
  { name: 'Apache Flink', what: 'Stateful stream processing with consistent checkpoints.' },
];
---
<Base title="About" description="About Siva Balan: software engineer and NYU MS Computer Science student working on backend systems, AI infrastructure, and GPU programming.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>About</h1>
    </header>

    <section class="section" aria-label="Introduction">
      <div class="section-label">
        <p class="note">From India, now in New York.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="section-body about-text">
        <p>
          I started programming in 8th grade because I enjoyed solving problems. What kept me
          interested wasn't just getting the answer, but understanding why a particular algorithm
          worked and how it solved the problem efficiently. That curiosity took me from competitive
          programming and CS fundamentals to building production systems at Ezee.ai, where
          algorithms, databases, distributed systems, and performance became real engineering
          problems.
        </p>
        <p>
          At NYU, I've been going deeper into algorithms, distributed systems, machine learning,
          LLMs, and GPU programming. Now I'm looking for work where I can keep solving difficult
          problems, learn from experienced engineers, and build systems that are useful to real
          people.
        </p>
        <a class="story-link" href="/about/story">
          <span class="story-title">My story <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
          <span class="story-sub">The longer version, from 8th grade to NYU.</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="study-h">
      <div class="section-label">
        <h2 id="study-h">Systems I'm studying</h2>
        <p class="note">Reading notes, not expertise.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p class="intro-line">Papers I've read to understand the designs behind tools I use.</p>
        <dl class="rows">
          {papers.map((p) => (
            <div><dt>{p.name}</dt><dd>{p.what}</dd></div>
          ))}
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="cp-h">
      <div class="section-label">
        <h2 id="cp-h">Competitive programming</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>
          I represented NYU at the ICPC North America Greater New York Regional in October 2025.
          I'm rated 4 stars on CodeChef (max 1801) and practice regularly on Codeforces and
          LeetCode. Graph problems and dynamic programming are my favorites.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-text p {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 1.12rem + 0.45vw, 1.5rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.2em;
  }
  .story-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    text-decoration: none;
    min-width: min(100%, 22rem);
  }
  .story-title { display: block; font-size: 1.0625rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--accent); }
  .story-sub { display: block; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9375rem; margin-top: 0.15rem; }
  .story-link:hover .story-title { text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }
  .intro-line { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
</style>
